---
import { LIFETIME_MS } from '@/consts';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Flick">
  <!-- The code modifiers replace the plugin's default backticks with a tinted pill. -->
  <main
    class="mx-auto prose px-6 py-12 prose-slate dark:prose-neutral dark:prose-invert prose-a:text-accent prose-code:rounded prose-code:bg-hover prose-code:px-1 prose-code:py-0.5 prose-code:font-normal prose-code:before:content-none prose-code:after:content-none"
  >
    <h1>About Flick</h1>
    <p>
      Flick is a programming language we created to explore compiler design. The compiler is open source at{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/flick-lang/flick">github.com/flick-lang/flick</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      This sandbox lets you try Flick without installing the compiler. Each run compiles and runs your program on a
      fresh, isolated machine with no network access, and stops after {LIFETIME_MS / 1000} seconds.
    </p>

    <h2>Key language features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Static typing with type inference</li>
      <li>Functions, and <code>extern fn</code> declarations for calling C functions</li>
      <li>Simple control flow: <code>if</code>/<code>else</code> and <code>while</code> loops</li>
      <li>Integers of any width, such as <code>u8</code> and <code>i11</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Authors</h2>
    <p>Flick was created by Max Larsson and Thomas Breydo.</p>

    <p><a href="/">Back to the sandbox</a></p>
  </main>
</Layout>
